IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-s7-base`

-- ccc1-s7-aircraft-platforms-ships.l4 -- section 7 (Offences committed outside Canada, deemed committed in Canada), subsections (1) to (2.21):
-- aircraft, cultural property, fixed platforms and ships, nuclear terrorism.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- SHAPE of each subsection: "every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission that if committed in Canada would be [offence]
-- ... shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if it is committed [(a) ... (g)]". The case the subsection is about (the lead-in)
-- is a scope limit: outside it the answer is NOTHING. The grounds (a) to (g) are an "if" gate: when the lead-in holds and no ground does,
-- the answer is JUST FALSE ("the subsection does not deem it committed in Canada"; another subsection may). A ground is a constructor named for its paragraph;
-- the facts are a LIST OF grounds, so "any of paragraphs (a) to (g)" is the list being non-empty.
-- The class of an offence, and the answers of section 2 and section 7(8), (9), are INPUTS (PLAN.md, seams R2 and R4): `Class of offence`, MAYBE BOOLEAN.

§ `Section 7(1) -- Offences committed on aircraft`

-- src:320 | Offences committed on aircraft
-- src:321 | 7 (1) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who
-- src:322 | (a) on or in respect of an aircraft
-- src:323 | (i) registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act, or
-- src:324 | (ii) leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft registered in Canada under those regulations,
-- src:325 | while the aircraft is in flight, or
-- src:326 | (b) on any aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight if the flight terminated in Canada,
-- src:327 | commits an act or omission in or outside Canada that if committed in Canada would be an offence punishable by indictment shall be deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada.
@ref s 7(1) (src:320-327)
DECLARE `s 7(1) the aircraft` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(1)(a)(i) an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act`
    `s 7(1)(a)(ii) an aircraft leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft registered in Canada under those regulations`
    `s 7(1)(b) any other aircraft`
    `s 7(1) not an aircraft`

@ref s 7(1) (src:320-327)
GIVEN aircraft IS A `s 7(1) the aircraft`
      `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the flight terminated in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` IS A `Class of offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF aircraft EQUALS `s 7(1) not an aircraft` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on or in respect of an aircraft"
        IF `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would be an offence punishable by indictment"
        IF `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 7(8) does not say whether the aircraft is in flight at that instant
        IF `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while the aircraft is in flight"
        IF aircraft EQUALS `s 7(1)(b) any other aircraft` AND NOT `the flight terminated in Canada` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while the aircraft is in flight if the flight terminated in Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 7(2) -- Offences against aircraft, air navigation facilities and airports`

-- src:328 | Idem
-- src:329 | (2) Notwithstanding this Act or any other Act, every one who
-- src:330 | (a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight, commits an act or omission outside Canada that if committed in Canada or on an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act would be an offence against section 76 or paragraph 77(a),
-- src:331 | (b) in relation to an aircraft in service, commits an act or omission outside Canada that if committed in Canada would be an offence against any of paragraphs 77(c), (d) or (g),
-- src:332 | (c) in relation to an air navigation facility used in international air navigation, commits an act or omission outside Canada that if committed in Canada would be an offence against paragraph 77(e),
-- src:333 | (d) at or in relation to an airport serving international civil aviation, commits an act or omission outside Canada that if committed in Canada would be an offence against paragraph 77(b) or (f), or
-- src:334 | (e) commits an act or omission outside Canada that if committed in Canada would constitute a conspiracy or an attempt to commit an offence referred to in this subsection, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to such an offence,
-- src:335 | shall be deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if the person is, after the commission thereof, present in Canada.
@ref s 7(2) (src:328-335)
DECLARE `s 7(2) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight`
    `s 7(2)(b) in relation to an aircraft in service`
    `s 7(2)(c) in relation to an air navigation facility used in international air navigation`
    `s 7(2)(d) at or in relation to an airport serving international civil aviation`
    `s 7(2) none of those circumstances`

@ref s 7(2) (src:328-335)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      circumstance IS A `s 7(2) circumstance`
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      relation IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence`
      `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the aircraft is in service, by s 7(9)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is, after the commission, present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission has none of those relations to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would be an offence against"
        IF NOT `the case is within a paragraph of the subsection` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "section 76 or paragraph 77(a)" "any of paragraphs 77(c), (d) or (g)" "paragraph 77(e)" "paragraph 77(b) or (f)"
        IF `the circumstance is paragraph (a)` AND `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 7(8) does not say whether the aircraft is in flight at that instant
        IF `the circumstance is paragraph (a)` AND `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while the aircraft is in flight"
        IF `the circumstance is paragraph (b)` AND `the aircraft is in service, by s 7(9)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 7(9) does not say whether the aircraft is in service at that instant
        IF `the circumstance is paragraph (b)` AND `the aircraft is in service, by s 7(9)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an aircraft in service"
        IF `the person is, after the commission, present in Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if the person is, after the commission thereof, present in Canada"
    WHERE
        `the offence is one referred to in the subsection` MEANS
            `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 76
            OR (`s 7 the offence is in section` offence 77 AND (offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(a)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(b)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(c)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(d)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(e)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(f)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(g)"))
        `the circumstance is paragraph (a)` MEANS
            relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission would be the offence itself` AND circumstance EQUALS `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight`
        `the circumstance is paragraph (b)` MEANS
            relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission would be the offence itself` AND circumstance EQUALS `s 7(2)(b) in relation to an aircraft in service`
        `the case is within a paragraph of the subsection` MEANS
            IF relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission would be the offence itself`
            THEN CONSIDER circumstance
                 WHEN `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` THEN `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 76 OR `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 77 "(a)"
                 WHEN `s 7(2)(b) in relation to an aircraft in service` THEN `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 77 "(c)" OR `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 77 "(d)" OR `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 77 "(g)"
                 WHEN `s 7(2)(c) in relation to an air navigation facility used in international air navigation` THEN `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 77 "(e)"
                 WHEN `s 7(2)(d) at or in relation to an airport serving international civil aviation` THEN `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 77 "(b)" OR `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 77 "(f)"
                 WHEN `s 7(2) none of those circumstances` THEN FALSE
            ELSE `the offence is one referred to in the subsection`

§ `Section 7(2.01) and (2.02) -- Offences in relation to cultural property`

-- src:336 | Offences in relation to cultural property
-- src:337 | (2.01) Despite anything in this Act or any other Act, a person who commits an act or omission outside Canada that if committed in Canada would constitute an offence under section 322, 341, 344, 380, 430 or 434 in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1 of the Convention, or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit such an offence, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to such an offence, is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if the person
-- src:338 | (a) is a Canadian citizen;
-- src:339 | (b) is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada; or
-- src:340 | (c) is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act and is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada.
@ref s 7(2.01) (src:336-340)
DECLARE `s 7(2.01) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(2.01)(b) the person is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada`
    `s 7(2.01)(c) the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act and is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada`

@ref s 7(2.01) (src:336-340)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      relation IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence`
      `it is in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1 of the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(2.01) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF NOT (`s 7 the offence is in section` offence 322 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 341 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 344 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 380 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 430 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 434) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 322, 341, 344, 380, 430 or 434"
        IF relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission has none of those relations to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit such an offence, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to such an offence"
        IF NOT `it is in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1 of the Convention` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1 of the Convention"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if the person"

-- src:341 | Definition of Convention
-- src:342 | (2.02) For the purpose of subsection (2.01), Convention means the Convention for the Protection of Cultural Property in the Event of Armed Conflict, done at The Hague on May 14, 1954. Article 1 of the Convention is set out in the schedule to the Cultural Property Export and Import Act.
@ref s 7(2.02) (src:341-342)
GIVEN `it is the Convention for the Protection of Cultural Property in the Event of Armed Conflict, done at The Hague on May 14, 1954` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.02) the instrument is the Convention` MEANS
    IF `it is the Convention for the Protection of Cultural Property in the Event of Armed Conflict, done at The Hague on May 14, 1954`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Convention means the Convention for the Protection of Cultural Property in the Event of Armed Conflict, done at The Hague on May 14, 1954."

-- "Article 1 of the Convention is set out in the schedule to the Cultural Property Export and Import Act": a pointer, carried as the text of where to find it.
@ref s 7(2.02) (src:342-342)
`s 7(2.02) where Article 1 of the Convention is set out` MEANS "the schedule to the Cultural Property Export and Import Act"

§ `Section 7(2.1) and (2.2) -- Fixed platforms and international maritime navigation`

-- src:343 | Offences against fixed platforms or international maritime navigation
-- src:344 | (2.1) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who commits an act or omission outside Canada against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of any state or against or on board a ship navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state, that if committed in Canada would constitute an offence against, a conspiracy or an attempt to commit an offence against, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to an offence against, section 78.1, shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if it is committed
-- src:345 | (a) against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of Canada;
-- src:346 | (b) against or on board a ship registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament;
-- src:347 | (c) by a Canadian citizen;
-- src:348 | (d) by a person who is not a citizen of any state and who ordinarily resides in Canada;
-- src:349 | (e) by a person who is, after the commission of the offence, present in Canada;
-- src:350 | (f) in such a way as to seize, injure or kill, or threaten to injure or kill, a Canadian citizen; or
-- src:351 | (g) in an attempt to compel the Government of Canada to do or refrain from doing any act.
@ref s 7(2.1) (src:343-351)
DECLARE `s 7(2.1) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(2.1)(a) the act or omission is committed against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of Canada`
    `s 7(2.1)(b) the act or omission is committed against or on board a ship registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament`
    `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(2.1)(d) the act or omission is committed by a person who is not a citizen of any state and who ordinarily resides in Canada`
    `s 7(2.1)(e) the act or omission is committed by a person who is, after the commission of the offence, present in Canada`
    `s 7(2.1)(f) the act or omission is committed in such a way as to seize, injure or kill, or threaten to injure or kill, a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(2.1)(g) the act or omission is committed in an attempt to compel the Government of Canada to do or refrain from doing any act`

@ref s 7(2.1) (src:343-351)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of any state, or a ship navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      relation IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence`
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(2.1) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF NOT `it is against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of any state, or a ship navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of any state or against or on board a ship navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state"
        IF NOT `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 78.1 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "section 78.1"
        IF relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission has none of those relations to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence against, a conspiracy or an attempt to commit an offence against, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to an offence against"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if it is committed"

-- src:352 | Offences against fixed platforms or navigation in the internal waters or territorial sea of another state
-- src:353 | (2.2) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who commits an act or omission outside Canada against or on board a fixed platform not attached to the continental shelf of any state or against or on board a ship not navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state, that if committed in Canada would constitute an offence against, a conspiracy or an attempt to commit an offence against, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to an offence against, section 78.1, shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada
-- src:354 | (a) if it is committed as described in any of paragraphs (2.1)(b) to (g); and
-- src:355 | (b) if the offender is found in the territory of a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is
-- src:356 | (i) a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship, or
-- src:357 | (ii) a party to the Protocol for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Fixed Platforms Located on the Continental Shelf, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a fixed platform.
@ref s 7(2.2) (src:352-357)
DECLARE `s 7(2.2)(b) the state in which the offender is found` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship`
    `s 7(2.2)(b)(ii) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Protocol for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Fixed Platforms Located on the Continental Shelf, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a fixed platform`
    `s 7(2.2)(b) a state that is none of those`

@ref s 7(2.2) (src:352-357)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is against or on board a fixed platform not attached to the continental shelf of any state, or a ship not navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      relation IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence`
      `the ways in which it is committed, as described in paragraphs (2.1)(a) to (g)` IS A LIST OF `s 7(2.1) ground`
      `the state in which the offender is found` IS A `s 7(2.2)(b) the state in which the offender is found`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF NOT `it is against or on board a fixed platform not attached to the continental shelf of any state, or a ship not navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against or on board a fixed platform not attached to the continental shelf of any state or against or on board a ship not navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state"
        IF NOT `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 78.1 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "section 78.1"
        IF relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission has none of those relations to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence against, a conspiracy or an attempt to commit an offence against, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to an offence against"
        IF NOT `paragraph (a) is met` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is committed as described in any of paragraphs (2.1)(b) to (g)"
        IF `the state in which the offender is found` EQUALS `s 7(2.2)(b) a state that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the offender is found in the territory of a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) is met` MEANS
            any (GIVEN g YIELD NOT (g EQUALS `s 7(2.1)(a) the act or omission is committed against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of Canada`)) `the ways in which it is committed, as described in paragraphs (2.1)(a) to (g)`

§ `Section 7(2.21) -- Nuclear terrorism offences committed outside Canada`

-- src:358 | Nuclear terrorism offence committed outside Canada
-- src:359 | (2.21) Despite anything in this Act or any other Act, everyone who commits an act or omission outside Canada that if committed in Canada would constitute an offence under any of sections 82.3 to 82.6, or a conspiracy or attempt to commit such an offence, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to such an offence, is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if
-- src:360 | (a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, under any Act of Parliament;
-- src:361 | (b) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft that
-- src:362 | (i) is registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act, or
-- src:363 | (ii) is leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations;
-- src:364 | (c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen; or
-- src:365 | (d) the person who commits the act or omission is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada.
@ref s 7(2.21) (src:358-365)
DECLARE `s 7(2.21) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(2.21)(a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, under any Act of Parliament`
    `s 7(2.21)(b)(i) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft that is registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act`
    `s 7(2.21)(b)(ii) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft that is leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations`
    `s 7(2.21)(c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(2.21)(d) the person who commits the act or omission is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada`

@ref s 7(2.21) (src:358-365)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      relation IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence`
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(2.21) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF NOT `s 7 the offence is in the range of sections` offence 82.3 82.6 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under any of sections 82.3 to 82.6"
        IF relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission has none of those relations to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or a conspiracy or attempt to commit such an offence, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to such an offence"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if"
